# {{ project_name }}

An open-lakehouse project scaffolded with [trestle](https://github.com/open-lakehouse/trestle).

## What this is

A project skeleton for an app that targets a lakehouse environment. The code and
proto live here; the local composed dev environment (Envoy gateway, storage,
catalog, ML tracking, …) is created separately with `trestle env`.

## Quickstart

```bash
# 1. Create the local composed environment (pick modules + set their knobs).
#    Rendered under ./env with an editable env.toml.
trestle env new {{ project_name }} --out-dir env

# 2. Bring it up.
cd env && docker compose up -d && cd ..

# 3. Regenerate code from proto as you iterate.
trestle generate
```

Run `trestle env list-modules --knobs` to see the available modules and the
configuration each exposes, and `trestle env render env` to re-render the
environment after editing `env/env.toml`.

